    "aqTRo64n8XY": {
      "result": "verified_selected_lines",
      "notes": "Seven branches, 19 exact positions from the complete five-piece source root. d7 ...Be8 d8=B leaves the defender mobile, then ...Ba4 Bf7 ...Bb5 Be7# mates. Against ...Bf7, immediate Bxf7 stalemates; Be7+ first gives actual Bb5 mate after ...Ke8, or a checked two-bishop win after ...Kg8 Bxf7+. Queen and rook promotion stalemate, knight promotion ...Ba4 draws. All encoded intermediate positions checked. The opening pawn is in motion in image 1: d6 is reconstructed from its highlighted origin before d7, with the next stable diagram confirming d7. Promoted Bd8 is dark-square; Bc4 and Black\u2019s bishop are light-square.",
